What PaperRust takes from paperless-ngx (v3.4.2, git submodule `upstream/`, unmodified):
- behaviour and business logic, ported from Python to Rust (each ported file names its upstream
  source in its header comment, see UPSTREAM_MAP.md),
- the database schema (Django migrations), reproduced in crates/pl-dbmigrate/schema and crates/pl-cli,
- the layout, styles and translation texts of its web UI (upstream/src-ui), which PaperRust's own
  Svelte UI (frontend-light/) was modelled on; the Angular UI itself is no longer shipped
  (retired 2026-11-13, see docs/FRONTEND-PARITY.md),
- parts of the user documentation (docs/user/), adapted.

The light web UI (frontend-light/) uses its own stylesheets, not those of paperless-ngx. It uses
Bootstrap and Bootstrap Icons (MIT) as npm packages.

