HEIC/HEIF photos (crates/pl-pdftools feature "heif", program paperrust-pdftool) are decoded with
craft-heif from craft-libs (https://github.com/storytold/craft-libs, revision
6e03f65bf45181db77ba6229716e6624db9eb25b, MIT OR Apache-2.0), which uses heic-rs 0.1.4
(https://crates.io/crates/heic-rs, MIT OR Apache-2.0, (c) the heic-rs authors), an independent
implementation of HEIF (ISO/IEC 23008-12) and of the HEVC decoding process (ITU-T H.265) written from
the published specifications. heic-rs does not grant any patent licence to the HEVC standard itself.
Both are unmodified dependencies used under the MIT license terms (GPL-3.0 compatible); the heic-rs
license text and its notice are in crates/pl-pdftools/licenses/heic-rs/, the craft-libs license text
in crates/pl-pdftools/licenses/wordcraft/LICENSE-MIT-craft-libs.

Relative date words in filters (crates/pl-docfilter/src/relative_dp_data.rs) are generated by
tools/gen_relative_dateparser.py from the language data of dateparser 1.4.3
(https://github.com/scrapinghub/dateparser, BSD-3-Clause, (c) Scrapinghub), which itself builds on
Unicode CLDR data (Unicode License v3). The data is used unmodified in content and converted to Rust;
the BSD-3-Clause and Unicode license texts apply to that file.

